From b839fa9d76352a3552f01c0ce2aa0ece2a1e2fc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:12:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Remembered rows: retire a removed worker's copy of
 another gateway's card; close a card that left a live owner's scope

Problem: 2026-11-18, after 6721503d602 and e9c07f61d27. Hub chats still listed 44 cards as open "on" removed
workers and 20 as unknown; MacBook chats 67 and 48.

Why 1 (open rows): they are remembered rows naming a removed worker as owner. The shared board shows 36 of the
hub's 44 done or archived and 7 alive on the hub: the worker node had published its copy of a hub card as its own.
Why 2: `_retire_moved` retires such a copy only on proof from the named owner (its scope read cleanly without the
card). A removed owner can never give that proof.
Why 1 (unknown rows): remembered rows last reported done or archived whose record left publication (a collector
publishes an archived card for 14 days) while the owner is alive: one missing record, so "absence is never
closure" kept them.
Root (happened): both rules predate machine removal and the publication window; neither had a case for "the owner
is gone but the real owner publishes the card" or "a live owner's clean scope no longer has a card that was
already closed".
Root (not caught): no test removed a worker that had published copies, or aged a closed card out of a live scope.

Fix (`_release_removed_owners`, fresh replica only, qualified unreleased rows):
- owner gone (publishes no task record, no fresh scope heartbeat) and another gateway publishes a record with the
  same board, id and created_at: the row is retired, that record speaks for the card. Any reported status.
- owner alive, its exact (profile, board) scope read cleanly and fresh, no record of the card from that gateway,
  and the row's last report was done or archived: released as reported (`aged_out`). A card last reported open
  is never closed by absence.
Both, like `owner_removed`, are re-made on every fresh read: a row carrying either marker is first put back to
unknown. Changed expectation: an owner that comes back with a clean fresh read of the scope and no such card now
keeps the card closed as `aged_out` (was: unknown); without a clean fresh read of that scope it is unknown as
before. `remembered_publications` also resolves publications for rows of gateways with no live scope.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_release_removed_owner_rows.py, through `_legacy_remote_links` on a real
replica file: a removed owner's copies are retired when another gateway publishes the same card and kept when the
created_at differs or nobody publishes it; a live owner's archived card that left its scope is released, its
running card is not, and a stale heartbeat takes the release back; an owner back with a clean scope keeps a done
card closed, and without one (scope error, other board, stale beat) it is unknown again.
Untested: the Desktop render; a card moved to another board of the same gateway.

